# The push-only script publishes the commit it was prepared for, and only
# while the derivation still admits it.
#
# The fixture prepares the script with the REAL `le commit push` over a
# commit P, lands another commit, runs the script, and asserts the bare
# upstream holds P and not the later commit (D-6, AC-5). It then prepares a
# script again, moves the upstream to a commit P does not descend from, runs
# the script, and asserts it exits non-zero and the upstream stayed where it
# was moved (AC-6): the script's `debt-status commit <P>` line is what stops
# it. No verify record exists at any point: a push owes none.
#
# Spec: spec-verification-debt-derived (closed; design in docs/architecture/testing/verify-freshness-scope.md).
# Delete the re-check line from the push-only script (internal/le/commit/script.go)
# and seq=1 fails at script-refused-when-upstream-moved.

option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture runner/commit-push-script-rechecks
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=script-pushed-the-prepared-commit
expect=stdout:contains=script-refused-when-upstream-moved
